schema: "0.4"
id: scholar-05-flashcard-decks-and-review
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal study CLI. Flashcard Decks & Review — SM-2 spaced-repetition
# practice (decks, due queue, front/back review, recall grading). Scholar's PRECISE-MINIMAL
# take in a LIGHT terminal (the deliberate contrast to chalkboard's hand-drawn teaching board).
# Theme tenets: light-native near-white canvas, single indigo accent, crisp 4px radius, thin
# visible gray borders (structure from lines), Inter prose + JetBrains Mono counts/codes.
# Palette: canvas #fafafa, ink #111118, alt #f5f5f5, border #e0e0e0, indigo accent #6366F1.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a clean,
    minimal LIGHT terminal window running a spaced-repetition flashcard review. This is
    Scholar's precise, exacting take — crisp and legible, the card foreground and everything
    else receding; deliberately NOT a hand-drawn chalkboard. Near-white terminal canvas (a
    light-mode terminal), NOT dark. Clean humanist sans (Inter) for the prompt and answer;
    a matched monospace for the search prompt, due/total counts, the queue counter and code
    strips. One single indigo accent; everything else near-neutral gray.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a clean, minimal LIGHT terminal window — "The Robot
    Learns" — running a spaced-repetition flashcard review. One near-white terminal pane
    fills the frame — the ENTIRE window background is bright, near-white paper (a light-theme
    terminal, like a bright light-mode IDE), dark ink on a light canvas, emphatically NOT a dark
    terminal and NOT a browser page, and precise and crisp — not a hand-drawn chalkboard.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (a title bar, a deck bar, a queue-progress line, then the active card):
    - TITLE BAR: minimal terminal chrome — three small dots and a mono title
      "the-robot-learns — /flashcard review".
    - DECK BAR: a SEARCH INPUT BAR (a bordered field with a mono prompt "find deck") beside
      two or three DECK SUMMARY TILES — small bordered chips each showing a deck name and a
      mono due/total count "Kubernetes 12/240", "Rust 3/88" — the active deck's chip carrying
      an indigo underline.
    - QUEUE PROGRESS: a "Card 6 of 18 due today" milestone tracker — a thin indigo bar on a
      recessed gray track beside a mono counter.
    - ACTIVE FLASHCARD (dominant): a single bordered near-white review card with 4px corners
      — the front prompt in medium-weight sans ("What does an Ingress do in Kubernetes?"), a
      thin divider, then the revealed back answer in muted prose with a small mono code strip;
      below the card a GRADE ROW of four bordered ghost buttons "again · hard · good · easy",
      the "good" button in an indigo-filled selected state.

    A faint mono status line: "SM-2 schedule · forgotten topics auto-resurface · e export deck".

    PALETTE & TYPE: near-white canvas; deep near-black ink for the front prompt; muted gray
    for the revealed answer and meta; a single saturated indigo as the only color — the
    queue-progress fill, the active-deck underline, the selected grade button, the caret.
    Prompt and answer in a clean humanist sans; the search prompt, due/total counts, the
    counter and the code strip in a matched monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: crisp small 4px rounded corners on the review card, deck chips, search
    field and grade buttons; thin visible cool-gray borders do the structural work (this
    theme earns clarity from lines, not shadow); flat surfaces with at most one very faint
    soft shadow on the review card. No gradients, no glow, no texture.

    MOOD: precise, exacting, calm — crisp minimal recall practice where the card is
    foreground and everything else recedes.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, web page, dark terminal, dark mode, black background, neon glow, gradient background, hand-drawn, chalk texture, sketchy, multiple accent colors"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Flashcard Decks & Review: a deck search bar with deck-summary tiles (due/total counts), a today's-queue progress tracker, a front/back review card, and an again/hard/good/easy grade row — inside a terminal pane"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Light-native near-white terminal canvas, a single indigo accent (no second saturated hue), crisp 4px radius, thin visible gray borders, Inter prose + monospace for counts/codes — precise and minimal, deliberately NOT hand-drawn and NOT a dark terminal"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Deck bar over a queue-progress line over the dominant review card with a grade row; clear hierarchy; plausible real-product terminal layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "dark terminal / dark mode instead of a light near-white terminal"
    - "hand-drawn, sketchy, or chalk-texture styling instead of crisp precise UI"
    - "more than one saturated accent hue"

tags: [scholar, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, terminal, hero]
